# PROJECT_CONTEXT.md — [project name]

*Claude: read this alongside `SE_Discipline.md` before any work. Human: fill in the sections below
before the first `/openspec-propose`. Blank sections mean Claude cannot tell "decided" from
"plausible-but-guessed" — leave things marked "TBD, ask before assuming" rather than inventing them.*

This is the **Track S (pure-software) context template** — for work where *you already know what to
build* and can supply the acceptance/golden cases yourself. It deliberately omits business-context /
requirements sections.

> **Building for a business need that isn't defined yet?** (business rules unknown at the outset,
> golden cases must be elicited from a business owner) — that's **Track E**. Turn on the optional
> product-definition front-end (`product-definition/`, upgrade Phase 5), which adds the full
> business-context, rules, and requirement-owner sections and hands its output into
> `/openspec-propose`. See `Plans/PLAN_ZZ_Upgrade_01.md`.

